---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FeedbackWidget from '../components/FeedbackWidget.astro';
---
<Layout title="Episode 3 Lesson">
  <h1>Episode 3 lesson: trust the pipeline, not the prompt</h1>
  <p>
    Episode 3 focuses on the work that happens after AI drafts code. The lesson is simple:
    AI can accelerate implementation, but trustworthy shipping comes from review, security
    checks, and deployment gates that make every change observable.
  </p>

  <div class="card">
    <strong>Talking point.</strong> Treat AI output as a starting point, then let independent
    controls decide whether the change is ready to ship.
  </div>

  <h2>Three questions before shipping</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Review:</strong> Did a separate reviewer inspect the change and its intent?</li>
    <li><strong>Secure:</strong> Did dependency, secret, and workflow checks run before release?</li>
    <li><strong>Deploy:</strong> Did automation promote only the version that passed those gates?</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This demo site models that loop: an issue creates a change, review and security checks
    harden it, and GitHub Actions handles the path to GitHub Pages.
  </p>

  <FeedbackWidget />
</Layout>
